WEBVTT

00:00:13.630 --> 00:00:16.850
That Jack the Ripper incident
that took place the other day--

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:20.060
when a common enemy appeared
before both the Yard and the public,

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:22.600
moments before they were
about to come to blows,

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:26.900
their hostility turned to solidarity
in the blink of an eye.

00:00:28.270 --> 00:00:33.450
Might one say that this was a brief
glimpse of the Moriarty Plan?

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:38.030
Nonetheless, this incident...

00:00:38.030 --> 00:00:41.790
Indeed. It does not appear
to be over just yet.

00:00:41.790 --> 00:00:45.710
This "Jack the Ripper,"
who no longer even exists...

00:00:45.710 --> 00:00:48.880
...has been arrested by the Yard.

00:00:50.710 --> 00:00:55.180
It is obvious that this is a case of a
false charge due to fabricated evidence.

00:00:55.180 --> 00:00:59.470
Yes. The Yard has been disgraced
by allowing Jack to escape,

00:00:59.470 --> 00:01:03.230
and it is conceivable that they
would resort to these methods.

00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:06.310
So, what do we do?

00:01:06.310 --> 00:01:11.730
Set the innocent citizen free, and see
that whomever accused him falsely...

00:01:11.730 --> 00:01:15.570
...receives the reward that he deserves.

00:01:15.570 --> 00:01:19.950
Then... just as your younger
brother has chosen,

00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:24.290
we will allow the case to go
unsolved and forgotten.

00:01:25.790 --> 00:01:29.170
I wish you every success, Albert.

00:01:30.460 --> 00:01:34.720
You and your brothers
do fine work together.

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:38.550
Make sure that you carry on well
with your own brother.

00:01:38.550 --> 00:01:40.390
Heh...

00:01:40.390 --> 00:01:43.180
That all depends on him.

00:02:03.950 --> 00:02:08.040
<i>Tripped up by your twisted words</i>

00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:11.790
<i>I can't fall asleep at night</i>

00:02:11.790 --> 00:02:15.920
<i>Transfixed by your gaze</i>

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:18.970
<i>I feel your sickness inside</i>

00:02:18.970 --> 00:02:23.390
<i>Injured, I break down</i>

00:02:23.390 --> 00:02:26.770
<i>this never-ending punishment</i>

00:02:26.770 --> 00:02:31.150
<i>I feel your sins all the time</i>

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:35.730
<i>It's inescapable, take me away</i>

00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:39.320
<i>I don't feel your love</i>
<i>But I can give you love</i>

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:43.450
<i>Show me a dream that will stir me awake</i>

00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:47.080
<i>I don't feel your love</i>
<i>But I can give you love</i>

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:51.210
<i>Whenever I awaken, you fall apart</i>

00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:54.290
<i>Someday... (Free your soul)</i>

00:02:54.290 --> 00:02:58.630
<i>Find me (Free your mind)</i>

00:02:58.630 --> 00:03:02.090
<i>Steal your heart (Free your soul)</i>

00:03:02.090 --> 00:03:05.970
<i>Endlessly (Free your mind)</i>

00:03:05.970 --> 00:03:08.770
<i>I will scream aloud</i>

00:03:16.730 --> 00:03:18.240
"The Riot in New Scotland Yard"

00:03:16.730 --> 00:03:18.240
Send out Jack!

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:19.820
"The Riot in New Scotland Yard"

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:19.820
Hang him at once!

00:03:19.820 --> 00:03:21.570
"The Riot in New Scotland Yard"

00:03:19.820 --> 00:03:21.570
Bring him to justice right now!

00:03:21.570 --> 00:03:22.490
Bring him to justice right now!

00:03:23.530 --> 00:03:26.120
Hell of a commotion out there, eh?

00:03:27.410 --> 00:03:29.910
Paterson...

00:03:29.910 --> 00:03:34.170
It was a lot like this on Bloody Sunday.

00:03:34.170 --> 00:03:39.420
The town doctor they arrested
has a clean record.

00:03:39.420 --> 00:03:43.090
The officers who took their orders
from Chief Inspector Arterton

00:03:43.090 --> 00:03:47.720
apparently found evidence
that he was involved in the case.

00:03:47.720 --> 00:03:49.430
What do you think?

00:03:49.430 --> 00:03:52.480
Hmph, the fact that you're
asking the question at all

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:56.770
means you have doubts about
this show of an arrest, don't you?

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:01.280
Good day, Chief Inspector Arterton.

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:03.950
Have that rabble outside silenced at once!

00:04:03.950 --> 00:04:04.700
All of them?

00:04:04.700 --> 00:04:07.780
Just drag out two or three of the leaders!

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:10.540
Duff them up proper and toss them
back out as an example to the others!

00:04:10.540 --> 00:04:12.870
We can't do that, sir.

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:18.050
Our culprit in this case
is likely falsely accused.

00:04:18.050 --> 00:04:20.420
And the one behind it...

00:04:20.420 --> 00:04:23.590
...is Chief Inspector Arterton.

00:04:23.590 --> 00:04:26.090
Do you have any proof?

00:04:26.090 --> 00:04:29.390
After all, he is our boss in the Criminal
Investigation Department,

00:04:29.390 --> 00:04:31.810
the CID's top man.

00:04:41.860 --> 00:04:44.400
Arterton is a man who has used
some fairly heavy-handed

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:47.620
crime-solving methods to produce
results before, as well.

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:51.250
All of which has gotten him
promoted to where he is.

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:57.290
And now that Jack the Ripper got
away from him before his very eyes,

00:04:57.290 --> 00:05:00.750
it's only a matter of time
before heads start to roll.

00:05:00.750 --> 00:05:05.130
One might say that's ample motivation
to falsify some evidence.

00:05:05.130 --> 00:05:08.550
Are we going to let his attempt to save
his own skin go unchallenged?!

00:05:08.550 --> 00:05:11.390
This is Scotland Yard!

00:05:11.390 --> 00:05:13.140
Lower your voice.

00:05:13.140 --> 00:05:15.060
S-Sorry.

00:05:15.060 --> 00:05:18.690
So, how are you planning to
prove that this is a frame-up?

00:05:18.690 --> 00:05:20.520
Well, I...

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:24.900
It's probable that he will confess to
the crime within the next day or two

00:05:24.900 --> 00:05:27.990
from a script of Arterton's own writing.

00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:35.580
Have you ever heard of a secret
ledger that Arterton keeps?

00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:37.460
Secret ledger?

00:05:37.460 --> 00:05:40.420
That's it! There must be a great
deal of off-the-books money

00:05:40.420 --> 00:05:42.880
at work for this level of fabrication.

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:46.090
If we can track down any money
diverted from the investigation,

00:05:46.090 --> 00:05:49.220
that itself would be
evidence of a frame-up.

00:05:49.220 --> 00:05:52.640
Yeah. It would be definitive proof.

00:05:52.640 --> 00:05:57.140
The question, though,
is where would we find it?

00:05:57.140 --> 00:06:00.520
The classified materials room on
the fifth floor would be my wager.

00:06:00.520 --> 00:06:01.400
Hmm?

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:06.450
Arterton is in charge of it,
and you need his permission to enter.

00:06:06.450 --> 00:06:10.490
But getting in there without Arterton's
knowledge would be unachievable.

00:06:10.490 --> 00:06:15.160
Hmm, it's times like this that call
for you to turn to <i>him</i>, right?

00:06:15.160 --> 00:06:19.670
The great... consulting detective.

00:06:19.670 --> 00:06:22.090
Holmes?

00:06:23.840 --> 00:06:27.970
But I doubt he will show any
interest in a treasure hunt...

00:06:42.440 --> 00:06:46.900
Ah... I have been expecting you...

00:06:46.900 --> 00:06:48.700
...Mr Bonde.

00:06:49.990 --> 00:06:54.450
I took the liberty of having
everything ready to go in here.

00:06:54.450 --> 00:06:57.620
This will be an infiltration mission,

00:06:57.620 --> 00:07:01.080
so I increased the silent nature of
the weapon by using air pressure,

00:07:01.080 --> 00:07:03.790
rather than gunpowder, to fire the rounds.

00:07:03.790 --> 00:07:07.170
The bullets are loaded
with a sleeping agent,

00:07:07.170 --> 00:07:10.090
so if you shoot them into a wall,
the agent will be released

00:07:10.090 --> 00:07:14.510
and anyone nearby will be
knocked out in no time at all.

00:07:14.510 --> 00:07:19.890
Very nice. Thank you. Tell me, Herder...
that over there wouldn't be...?

00:07:19.890 --> 00:07:25.270
Ah, that caught your attention, did it?
You have a keen eye, Mr Bonde.

00:07:25.270 --> 00:07:29.110
Yes, I just got finished
putting this together...

00:07:32.320 --> 00:07:35.410
A specially built autocar!

00:07:44.290 --> 00:07:45.880
Excuse me, sir.

00:07:48.710 --> 00:07:51.220
Ames, what is it?

00:07:51.220 --> 00:07:55.180
The suspect's lawyer is here
and is demanding to meet with him.

00:07:55.180 --> 00:07:59.810
We can't have him getting any funny
ideas before we obtain his confession.

00:07:59.810 --> 00:08:03.770
Tell the lawyer that there's an emergency
or something and send him away.

00:08:03.770 --> 00:08:06.980
I'll have this all sewn up by morning!

00:08:06.980 --> 00:08:08.190
Yes, sir.

00:08:10.070 --> 00:08:12.400
He's on edge.

00:08:13.530 --> 00:08:18.080
Uh-oh, it's just about time
for my meeting with him.

00:08:25.130 --> 00:08:28.500
He's late. Is this man
not the punctual type?

00:09:02.660 --> 00:09:05.370
Sorry I'm late.

00:09:05.370 --> 00:09:07.960
Sir, what can I get you?

00:09:07.960 --> 00:09:10.750
Five parts brandy to one part maraschino,

00:09:10.750 --> 00:09:14.170
and once you've finished swirling it,
three dashes of Angostura bitters.

00:09:14.170 --> 00:09:18.390
Three dashes? Very good, sir.

00:09:18.390 --> 00:09:21.100
You're drawing a frightful
amount of attention.

00:09:21.100 --> 00:09:25.100
It took some time to explain the gear
and get approval to take it with me.

00:09:25.100 --> 00:09:26.560
But since I was able to borrow that,

00:09:26.560 --> 00:09:29.610
I made it here a lot quicker
than I would have in a carriage.

00:09:29.610 --> 00:09:32.440
Hmph, for heaven's sake.

00:09:32.440 --> 00:09:36.950
Right now, we are on high alert, thanks to
orders from Arterton at headquarters.

00:09:36.950 --> 00:09:40.490
It will require a double check
to get inside the building.

00:09:40.490 --> 00:09:44.290
I cannot sneak you inside on my own.

00:09:44.290 --> 00:09:49.840
Oh, come on now, luv. Yeah, you...

00:09:49.840 --> 00:09:52.090
The town doctor who is under suspicion

00:09:52.090 --> 00:09:55.420
has already undergone
harsh interrogation as it is.

00:09:55.420 --> 00:10:00.510
We need to resolve all of this
before they get a confession.

00:10:00.510 --> 00:10:03.310
Where is this secret ledger?

00:10:03.310 --> 00:10:06.060
We know it is in the
classified materials room,

00:10:06.060 --> 00:10:09.440
but as you need Arterton's
permission to enter,

00:10:09.440 --> 00:10:12.820
he has his own hand-picked
officers guarding it.

00:10:14.860 --> 00:10:18.160
Your as-yet-unnamed cocktail, sir. Enjoy.

00:10:18.160 --> 00:10:19.870
Thanks.

00:10:19.870 --> 00:10:24.660
That's no obstacle. There isn't
anything I've been unable to steal.

00:10:24.660 --> 00:10:26.620
That's most daring.

00:10:27.710 --> 00:10:31.380
Would you like one? It takes an already
acerbic drink and makes it harsher.

00:10:31.380 --> 00:10:34.130
You can really savour
the bitters this way.

00:10:34.130 --> 00:10:36.130
No, thank you.

00:10:38.510 --> 00:10:42.850
Mm, quite good. I think I'll
call this a "Paterson."

00:10:42.850 --> 00:10:47.100
As I said earlier, you have to
get inside headquarters first.

00:10:47.100 --> 00:10:50.230
What will you do?
Disguise yourself as Lestrade?

00:10:50.230 --> 00:10:51.520
No...

00:10:51.520 --> 00:10:53.230
What is the matter with you?!

00:10:53.230 --> 00:10:55.480
Sir, please stop this at once.

00:10:55.480 --> 00:10:57.070
Oh, why should I?
Let's have a drink together.

00:10:57.070 --> 00:10:57.780
--Please stop!

00:10:57.780 --> 00:10:59.030
--That won't be necessary.
--Please stop!

00:10:59.030 --> 00:10:59.820
--That won't be necessary.
--I said let's drink!

00:10:59.820 --> 00:11:01.370
--Don't touch me!
--I said let's drink!

00:11:01.370 --> 00:11:03.030
Stop fighting me!

00:11:04.910 --> 00:11:07.960
You are bothering the lady, mister.

00:11:07.960 --> 00:11:10.210
Wh-Why, you--!

00:11:10.210 --> 00:11:11.330
Thank you!

00:11:11.330 --> 00:11:13.340
My pleasure.

00:11:16.260 --> 00:11:19.550
Trifle with me, will you? I'll kill you!

00:11:26.310 --> 00:11:30.940
Because of the heightened security,
they can't be bothered with drunkards,

00:11:30.940 --> 00:11:35.230
so we're lucky their frisking
wasn't very thorough.

00:11:36.110 --> 00:11:38.740
We got inside the building, didn't we?

00:11:41.450 --> 00:11:43.240
I have good news.

00:11:43.240 --> 00:11:47.370
Lestrade just returned,
and he asked for me.

00:11:47.370 --> 00:11:51.120
He brought someone with him whom
he couldn't get admitted alone,

00:11:51.120 --> 00:11:53.670
thanks to the double checks.

00:11:53.670 --> 00:11:55.790
Which would mean...

00:11:55.790 --> 00:12:02.090
Yeah. Just as you hoped, it could
only be that consulting detective.

00:12:02.090 --> 00:12:07.010
All of the players are here.
It's time to begin the operation.

00:12:18.280 --> 00:12:22.030
That should be enough working him over.

00:12:22.030 --> 00:12:23.910
You can take it from here.

00:12:23.910 --> 00:12:25.530
Very well, sir.

00:12:48.100 --> 00:12:51.520
--Send out Jack! Send out Jack!
--Send out Jack! Send out Jack!

00:12:51.520 --> 00:12:53.440
--Send out Jack!
--Send out Jack!

00:12:53.440 --> 00:12:57.400
I'm impressed that you managed
to bring Holmes here, Lestrade.

00:12:57.400 --> 00:12:59.650
Yeah. I was surprised, as well,

00:12:59.650 --> 00:13:03.110
but before I could even explain
what was happening, he said...

00:13:03.110 --> 00:13:07.490
That is 100% a frame-up. I'll help you.

00:13:07.490 --> 00:13:09.080
...to me.

00:13:09.080 --> 00:13:11.160
I'm glad to hear it.

00:13:11.160 --> 00:13:14.410
Sherlock, I know it's
to exonerate this man,

00:13:14.410 --> 00:13:18.960
but are you certain you want to search
the Yard for a hidden ledger?

00:13:18.960 --> 00:13:23.590
John, I told you the true story behind
the Jack the Ripper case, right?

00:13:23.590 --> 00:13:26.430
There's something I need
to verify for myself.

00:13:26.430 --> 00:13:28.300
I see.

00:13:28.300 --> 00:13:31.810
It was the Lord of Crime
who solved that case,

00:13:31.810 --> 00:13:34.730
and if the Lord of Crime really
is playing Robin Hood,

00:13:34.730 --> 00:13:38.730
then he will most likely step in
concerning this unjustified arrest.

00:13:38.730 --> 00:13:41.860
But if I'm not careful about
how I go about this,

00:13:41.860 --> 00:13:43.820
I'll upset the chain of
events he has planned,

00:13:43.820 --> 00:13:47.360
and in the worst case, he will be unable
to rescue an innocent citizen.

00:13:49.990 --> 00:13:53.620
That miserable sod!
He infuriates me, every single time!

00:13:53.620 --> 00:13:57.540
He's no doubt accounted
for my behaviour in his plans!

00:13:57.540 --> 00:14:01.960
At no point do I have the luxury
of making any choices.

00:14:01.960 --> 00:14:06.630
The way things are going, I will be
trapped in the palm of his hand forever!

00:14:06.630 --> 00:14:08.010
Sherlock...

00:14:08.010 --> 00:14:09.430
Sherlock!

00:14:10.850 --> 00:14:13.350
The inspector is going
to show us upstairs.

00:14:13.350 --> 00:14:15.520
Hmm? Oh...

00:14:18.690 --> 00:14:23.900
I just have to make the choices that
I believe are right during this.

00:14:23.900 --> 00:14:27.280
Whether I'm in the palm
of his hand or not.

00:14:31.780 --> 00:14:36.250
Inspector Lestrade,
this is a restricted area.

00:14:36.250 --> 00:14:39.210
I have business in the
classified materials room.

00:14:40.380 --> 00:14:45.010
As you can see, I have the key given
to me by Chief Inspector Arterton.

00:14:45.010 --> 00:14:49.430
Which is a blatant lie that
Holmes put me up to...

00:14:49.430 --> 00:14:50.720
Holmes...

00:14:50.720 --> 00:14:52.140
Right.

00:14:53.220 --> 00:14:57.810
We had not been informed that
you were coming, Inspector.

00:14:57.810 --> 00:15:00.060
This is something that
came up rather suddenly.

00:15:00.060 --> 00:15:02.440
So these two are...?

00:15:02.440 --> 00:15:04.110
Let's go.

00:15:04.110 --> 00:15:05.150
Inspector!

00:15:05.150 --> 00:15:07.070
These two are helping
with the investigation.

00:15:07.070 --> 00:15:10.910
They also have Chief Inspector
Arterton's authorization.

00:15:10.910 --> 00:15:13.330
The chief inspector gave
his key to the inspector?

00:15:13.330 --> 00:15:14.950
Did you hear anything about this?

00:15:14.950 --> 00:15:16.410
No.

00:15:16.410 --> 00:15:18.750
That's the room.

00:15:18.750 --> 00:15:20.210
You're on, Holmes.

00:15:20.210 --> 00:15:22.790
Yeah, I'll handle it.

00:15:24.340 --> 00:15:26.090
Sherlock...!

00:15:31.220 --> 00:15:32.470
Hold it!

00:15:34.300 --> 00:15:36.220
That was fast.

00:15:38.480 --> 00:15:41.310
I'm sure you can explain
yourself, right, Lestrade?

00:15:41.310 --> 00:15:43.400
During this time of emergency,
of all things,

00:15:43.400 --> 00:15:45.610
you not only enter a restricted
area without my permission,

00:15:45.610 --> 00:15:47.730
but you bring civilians in with you!

00:15:47.730 --> 00:15:51.450
Answer me! What are you plotting?!

00:15:52.450 --> 00:15:55.910
Are we going to let his attempt to save
his own skin go unchallenged?!

00:15:55.910 --> 00:15:59.330
This is Scotland Yard!

00:15:59.330 --> 00:16:03.080
This case needs to be re-examined.

00:16:03.080 --> 00:16:04.790
What did you say?

00:16:06.090 --> 00:16:11.630
I believe... that the man who was
arrested has been wrongly accused!

00:16:11.630 --> 00:16:14.600
You would dare to defy me?

00:16:14.600 --> 00:16:18.270
There is a secret ledger somewhere
in this room that will substantiate

00:16:18.270 --> 00:16:20.980
that you falsified the
evidence, isn't there?

00:16:22.520 --> 00:16:25.310
There is no false accusation!

00:16:25.310 --> 00:16:28.070
If I say there isn't one,
then there isn't one!

00:16:28.070 --> 00:16:31.360
And I will never give you
my permission to go in there!

00:16:31.360 --> 00:16:36.830
If you attempt to break in here again,
then I will arrest you without delay!

00:16:36.830 --> 00:16:40.000
From his reaction,
there can be no question.

00:16:40.000 --> 00:16:42.580
The ledger is in there.

00:16:51.970 --> 00:16:53.760
I-Inspector!

00:16:54.840 --> 00:16:58.310
I am not going to let you turn
an innocent man into a criminal!

00:16:59.720 --> 00:17:02.310
He really steps up when
he wants to, doesn't he?

00:17:03.640 --> 00:17:05.310
Let me go!

00:17:06.230 --> 00:17:11.150
Someone go and get more help!
Toss Lestrade into a cell!

00:17:11.150 --> 00:17:12.360
Yes, sir.

00:17:24.330 --> 00:17:25.920
Let's go, John.

00:17:25.920 --> 00:17:28.500
Huh? But what about Inspector Lestrade?

00:17:28.500 --> 00:17:30.170
It's no matter.

00:17:43.980 --> 00:17:45.730
Oof...

00:17:48.150 --> 00:17:53.610
My word, this certainly is a day
for my friends to be thrown in here.

00:17:53.610 --> 00:17:54.820
Paterson?

00:17:54.820 --> 00:17:57.490
That was much too rash, Lestrade.

00:17:57.490 --> 00:17:58.950
I'm so ashamed.

00:17:58.950 --> 00:18:01.740
Heh, it's also just like you.

00:18:01.740 --> 00:18:03.410
I brought you something.

00:18:05.120 --> 00:18:08.380
You mean, that's-- It can't be!

00:18:08.380 --> 00:18:10.630
Arterton's secret ledger.

00:18:10.630 --> 00:18:14.170
Whilst you were having your donnybrook
in the classified materials room,

00:18:14.170 --> 00:18:17.180
I dipped into his office and found it.

00:18:17.180 --> 00:18:20.550
You're saying that it was never
in there to begin with.

00:18:23.390 --> 00:18:29.100
In hindsight, I ended up treating you
all as decoys. I'm sorry about that.

00:18:29.100 --> 00:18:34.860
Don't mention it. We're still achieving
the goal of saving an innocent man.

00:18:37.150 --> 00:18:40.990
All that remains now is for you
to give that to Holmes.

00:18:42.410 --> 00:18:47.040
The time to drag Arterton out
of the CID top spot has arrived.

00:18:47.040 --> 00:18:49.920
Yeah! Leave that to me, Paterson!

00:18:53.880 --> 00:18:58.010
It looks like it's going to work.
I have to say, though...

00:19:00.390 --> 00:19:03.930
Hell's bells... that chap is bloody mad.

00:19:06.140 --> 00:19:08.350
Still, he is good enough for
the gentleman to recognise

00:19:08.350 --> 00:19:13.980
and admit him into the
organisation, it would seem.

00:19:35.630 --> 00:19:38.050
Is that the article on that
wrongful accusation case?

00:19:38.050 --> 00:19:42.180
Yeah. It looks like the chief
inspector has been replaced.

00:19:42.180 --> 00:19:46.180
Word is that the officers who were his
cronies have all been disposed of, too.

00:19:47.310 --> 00:19:50.310
Nonetheless, it's a good thing that those
who were arrested on false charges

00:19:50.310 --> 00:19:52.350
have now been set free.

00:19:52.350 --> 00:19:55.270
Inspector Lestrade's courage
was surprising, as well.

00:19:55.270 --> 00:19:56.650
Yeah.

00:19:59.530 --> 00:20:04.780
The Jack the Ripper affair and
this case of false accusation...

00:20:04.780 --> 00:20:06.870
He secretly insinuated
himself into both cases

00:20:06.870 --> 00:20:09.660
and solved them both more
favourably than I would have.

00:20:09.660 --> 00:20:13.420
The truth to be derived from this...

00:20:13.420 --> 00:20:17.880
...is that he is a Robin Hood.
There can be no mistake in thinking that.

00:20:17.880 --> 00:20:21.430
But at the same time,
he is also a criminal.

00:20:21.430 --> 00:20:23.260
Was his objective

00:20:23.260 --> 00:20:29.430
solely to rescue an innocent citizen
and set him free in this case?

00:20:30.930 --> 00:20:33.690
What can I get for you, sir?

00:20:33.690 --> 00:20:35.480
Well, let's see...

00:20:35.480 --> 00:20:41.150
A brandy and maraschino,
with three dashes of Angostura bitters.

00:20:41.150 --> 00:20:43.200
Very good, sir.

00:20:43.200 --> 00:20:46.370
That's a most unusual drink you're having.

00:20:46.370 --> 00:20:49.540
Hmph, a friend of mine
likes drinking them.

00:20:49.540 --> 00:20:52.210
I want to know how they taste.

00:20:52.210 --> 00:20:53.710
I see.

00:20:53.710 --> 00:20:57.380
You know, I'm sorry things
turned out the way they did.

00:20:57.380 --> 00:21:00.420
Everyone else wanted you to do it.

00:21:00.420 --> 00:21:03.760
You are the hero who lanced
our collective boil, after all.

00:21:03.760 --> 00:21:07.220
When you put it that way,
<i>you're </i>the real hero.

00:21:07.220 --> 00:21:12.640
If it weren't for you, things wouldn't
have ended up the way they have.

00:21:12.640 --> 00:21:19.440
Besides... I want to get out and
pursue cases in the field a little more.

00:21:19.440 --> 00:21:23.820
Ha, that's just like you, Lestrade.

00:21:23.820 --> 00:21:26.820
Thank you for waiting.
Here is your Paterson.

00:21:26.820 --> 00:21:29.120
Huh?

00:21:29.120 --> 00:21:35.210
Sorry to end up sticking you with the
hassle of the chief inspector's post.

00:21:35.210 --> 00:21:39.090
Don't mention it. We're chums, aren't we?

00:21:39.090 --> 00:21:41.920
Congratulations on your
promotion, Paterson.

00:21:44.880 --> 00:21:47.470
Ugh, too bitter!

00:21:47.470 --> 00:21:49.640
The corruption within
the Yard has been purged,

00:21:49.640 --> 00:21:52.560
and the top CID post has been reassigned.

00:21:52.560 --> 00:21:55.770
We now have someone in the
chain of command at the Yard.

00:21:55.770 --> 00:22:01.690
He will be of great use to us
henceforth with our plans.

00:22:01.690 --> 00:22:07.030
The time to execute the
Moriarty Plan is coming soon.

00:22:07.360 --> 00:22:14.660
<i>Fate that over time changes</i>
<i>into chains of sorrow,</i>

00:22:14.660 --> 00:22:22.880
<i>leave me the light of rebirth</i>
<i>for the world ahead</i>

00:22:29.510 --> 00:22:33.470
<i>Struck by a frustration</i>
<i>I'd never experienced before,</i>

00:22:33.470 --> 00:22:36.850
<i>I feel lost, I feel lost</i>

00:22:36.850 --> 00:22:40.860
<i>The letters I dashed off</i>
<i>are all I remember</i>

00:22:40.860 --> 00:22:44.230
<i>It's all true, it's all true</i>

00:22:44.230 --> 00:22:51.660
<i>Witness as I forgo my forsaken future</i>
<i>with no regrets</i>

00:22:51.660 --> 00:23:00.250
<i>and you will win your intent</i>
<i>at the expense of becoming my pawn</i>

00:23:02.250 --> 00:23:08.050
<i>A scarlet thread fluttering in the wind</i>
<i>at five in the morning</i>

00:23:08.050 --> 00:23:14.310
<i>I'll recover my memories on the last day</i>

00:23:14.310 --> 00:23:17.100
<i>Hold me down till the end</i>

00:23:17.100 --> 00:23:22.770
<i>Finish by wiping away my sins,</i>

00:23:22.770 --> 00:23:29.450
<i>warning me to stay true if I desire beauty</i>

00:23:44.500 --> 00:23:49.800
Next time on <i>Moriarty the Patriot</i>:
"The Merchant of London."
